---

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Prohibited misuse</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>No unlawful activity, sanctions evasion, or facilitation of attacks.</li>
    <li>No abuse, harassment, or distribution of malware through services that depend on the resolver.</li>
    <li>No scanning of, attacks against, or attempts to compromise SecretChip infrastructure.</li>
    <li>No attempts to bypass filtering, rate limits, abuse controls, or access restrictions.</li>
    <li>No excessive automated load or traffic patterns that materially impact platform health.</li>
    <li>No resale of the AEGIS PDNS resolver service without prior written permission from SecretChip.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Abuse handling</h2>
  <p>SecretChip may investigate abuse reports, request context, and coordinate remediation actions with affected parties or providers.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Right to restrict, suspend, or block</h2>
  <p>SecretChip may rate-limit, restrict, suspend, or block clients that violate this policy or that materially impact the integrity of the platform or other users.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Fair-use for public endpoints</h2>
  <p>Public endpoint access is subject to reasonable use expectations. Excessive automated load may be controlled.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Lawful use expectations</h2>
  <p>Users are responsible for compliance with applicable laws and regulations in their relevant jurisdictions.</p>
</div>
